=== HARNESS SOURCE ATTACK ===
Identity checks:
  harness.mjs: sign-in error is fatal; returned session.user.id is NOT compared to seed-map.
  attacks.mjs: sign-in error fatal; returned user id compared; mismatch fatal.
  scoping.mjs: sign-in error recorded as failure; returned user id compared; mismatch recorded as failure.
  revocation.mjs: sign-in error fatal; returned user id compared; mismatch fatal.

DENY classifier:
  verdictFromResult() maps ANY API error to DENY; it does not require 42501 for denied INSERT.
  zero returned/affected rows also maps to DENY.

Matrix mutation ground truth:
  320-cell matrix performs no service-role before/after ground truth for denied mutations.
  dedicated attacks ground-truth selected user_data, junction, account, and pbm_info mutations.
  attacks A7.1 reference INSERT has no service-role truth callback.
  attacks also accept any non-ALLOW outcome rather than requiring an operation-specific denial shape.

Missing-row mechanism:
  harness update/delete target = inserted row, per-identity target, static target, or sentinel dead UUID.
  payloads with null targets include user_roles, user_businesses, pending_registrations,
  apa_memberships, all five reference tables, audit_logs (profiles has a targetFor override).
  For expected-DENY UPDATE/DELETE cells on these tables, a missing target can yield zero affected
  even if a policy is over-permissive.

Non-vacuity and cleanup:
  seed.mjs seeds all sixteen matrix tables (baseline rows arise from the Auth trigger).
  matrix SELECT uses limit(5): presence/absence only, not exhaustive scope.
  scoping exact-checks user_data counts plus business/account name lists.
  matrix cleanup/restoration uses service role but does not fail the run on cleanup/restore errors;
  it counts only successful operations and does not ground-truth final shape for every table.

Volume and Auth cleanup:
  explicit volume claims use exact head counts in scoping/revocation/ground-truth paths.
  seed Auth cleanup calls listUsers({perPage:1000}) once; it does not paginate beyond 1,000.

Target selection:
  env loader chooses requested prefixed keys, then Amendment A-1 fallbacks.
  publishable==secret is rejected.
  prove.mjs supplies DB_RESET_ALLOW=yes automatically after env selection.
  db-reset requires DB_URL and the allow flag, but has no independent project/host allowlist.

AC8 direct execution:
  catalog privilege checks cover all four helpers.
  live anon execution probe calls only my_business_ids().

Seed-map/evidence coupling:
  seed.mjs rewrites tracked seed-map.json with current run ids.
  direct harness invocation can consume a stale map; prove.mjs stops if seed exits nonzero.

Normalization and labels:
  normalizer masks every UUID, timestamp, timing, token-fingerprint text, and duration.
  outcomes/counts and pooler host remain visible.
  UUID masking can conceal wrong-identity/tenant-id drift if a log relies only on identifiers.
  current prove.mjs accepts a phase label, but existing X6 consolidated evidence points to an X5-matrix sub-log.

Service role:
  centralized in lib/db.mjs; used by seed, matrix cleanup/restoration, attacks ground truth,
  and revocation mutation/truth. Matrix cells use publishable-key clients, not service role.

Additional instrument observations:
